    <div class="banner-wrap">
        <div class="page-width">
            <picture class="banner-picture">
                {% comment %} <source srcset="{{'storage-banner.png' |  file_img_url: '1200x'}}" media="(min-width: 768px) and (min-resolution: 2dppx)"> {% endcomment %}
                <img src="{{'storage-banner.png' |  file_img_url: '1200x'}}" width="" height="" loading="lazy" alt="More JasonL Office Furniture">
            </picture>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="introtxt">
        <div class="page-width">
            <h2>New mandatory standard for toppling furniture.</h2>
            <div class="intro-detail">
                <p><strong>Effective May 2025</strong>, a new mandatory Australian safety standard has been introduced to help prevent injuries and fatalities caused by furniture tip-overs. At JasonL, safety is core to how we design, source, and support our products — and we fully support this national initiative.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="toppling-content-detail">
        <div class="page-width main-content-wrap-border-top">
            <div class="main-content-wrap">
                <div class="column1">
                    <h4 class="headingtop">What’s changing?</h4>
                    <p>The Consumer Goods (Toppling Furniture) Information Standard 2024, introduced by the Australian Government, requires all suppliers of certain freestanding furniture to meet strict safety labelling and information requirements — both online and in-store.</p>

                    <h4>These new rules are in response to:</h4>
                    <ul class="number-list">
                        <li>
                            Over 28 deaths and 900+ injuries annually from toppling furniture incidents in Australia.
                        </li>
                        <li> 
                            Children under 5 and older adults being the most at-risk groups.
                        </li>
                    </ul>
                    <h4>Which furniture is affected?</h4>
                    <p>The standard applies to “Toppling Furniture,” which includes:</p>
                    <ul class="dot-list">
                        <li>Category 1: Clothes storage units and bookcases over 686mm height.</li>
                        <li>Category 2: Entertainment units.</li>
                        <li>Category 3: Hall tables, sideboards, display cabinets,  buffets and credenzas over 686mm in height.</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
                <div class="column2">
                    <div class="col-leftspace">
                        <h4 class="headingtop">What Jasonl is doing?</h4>
                        <p>At JasonL, we’ve updated our products and documentation to meet or exceed the new requirements:</p>
                        <ul class="dot-list">
                            <li>Clear, permanent warning labels are affixed to applicable furniture items.</li>
                            <li>Point-of-sale tags highlight safety risks and best practices in-store.</li>
                            <li>Assembly instructions now include a warning label and offer support on how to source and use a wall anchor.</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                    <div class="note-box">
                        <p>We’ve made these updates not just to comply, but because we sell to <strong>both businesses outfitting commercial spaces and individuals furnishing their homes.</strong> Whether it’s a bustling office or a family living room, safety matters — and we're committed to helping you create secure environments wherever our furniture is used.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
